      "content": "it's hard to believe anyone else sees it that way. everyone always talks about fighting, about clinging to the light, but it just feels so exhausting. so heavy. like i'm just dragging this body through the mud every single day. when you talk about surrender... it almost sounds like it's the only logical thing left to do. like the most beautiful thing one could actually achieve.",
